**S1 — done:** 200k raw fp16 residual-stream vectors/layer for layers {0,3,6,9,11} (912 seqs × 256 tokens, all positions pooled), in `data/`.

**S2 linear (PCA-PR) — done, all layers full 200k:** The headline so far is a real, known phenomenon — from layer 3 onward a single "massive-activation" outlier dimension carries **78–94%** of total variance, collapsing the raw participation ratio to ~1. The informative linear ID is the post-dominant spread: e.g. **layer 6 needs 94 dims for 95% and 479 for 99%** variance (≪768 but ≫1). Layer 0 is broad (PR=21.3).

**Next step (next iteration):** hand-roll TwoNN + MLE in pure numpy (torch.cdist/topk kNN on CPU, no skdim/sklearn) over 10k/50k subsamples per layer, then the S3 AE bottleneck sweep on layer 6.

On track? yes — S1 100%, S2 ~40%; ~45 min of the 240 used.
