## What I did this iteration
1. **S2b — nonlinear intrinsic dimension** (the blocker): rewrote `id_estimate.py` in pure numpy/torch (the old one imported `skdim`, which isn't installed) — TwoNN + MLE via chunked CPU `torch.cdist` kNN. **Validated** both on synthetic Gaussians of known dimension first, then ran all 5 layers × {10k,50k} × {centered, standardized} → `results/id_nonlinear.json`.
2. **S3 — AE bottleneck sweep** on layer 6. The original config (4000 steps × batch 4096) burned 22 min CPU on a single k — violating the "no run >10 min" rule — so I measured step time and re-sized to STEPS=1200/BATCH=2048 (identical across k, so the elbow comparison stays valid), then ran k∈{2…256} → `results/ae_results.json`.
3. **S4 — REPORT.md** + empty **STOP**.

## Headline result
The GPT-2 layer-6 residual stream is a **strongly-curved manifold of intrinsic dimension ≈12–16**, and the two independent estimates **agree**:

| Estimate | Value |
|---|---|
| Ambient (d_model) | 768 |
| Linear PCA d95 | 94 |
| **Nonlinear ID (TwoNN / MLE)** | **≈12 / ≈13** |
| **AE bottleneck elbow** | **≈16** |

So the stream is *linearly* spread over ~100 directions but *nonlinearly* compressible to ~12–16 — AE elbow ≈ nonlinear ID, both ~6× below linear d95 and ~50× below d_model. Nonlinear ID also grows gently with depth (6→~14), and standardization barely moves it, confirming the massive-activation outlier dim drives *global variance* but not *local geometry*.

`On track? yes — all stages S1–S4 complete, success criterion satisfied, STOP written.`

