## Summary of this iteration (Iter 7)

A new operator review (`CODEX_REVIEW_20260623T001526Z.md`, dated today) had appeared with STOP missing. I addressed every point:

**Ran new diagnostics** (`experiments/id_diagnostics.py`, GPU/RTX 3090, 8s → `results/id_diagnostics.json`):
- **#4 Duplicate/self-masking** — 92/50k exact dupes (0.18%); explicit self-index masking (vs the naive drop-smallest-distance) moves **TwoNN 0.00, MLE +0.17** → the low layer-6 ID is *not* a duplicate artifact.
- **rec#5 Bootstrap CIs** — **TwoNN 12.71±0.13, MLE 15.18±0.09** at n=20k. Sampling CI is tiny (±0.1); the real spread is finite-sample n-dependence (n=50k→20k), so the ID band is honestly **11–15**, not a single point.

**Documented one genuine correctness bug (#5):** `GPT2Model.hidden_states[L+1]` applies `ln_f` to its last entry, so **layer 11 is post-final-layernorm, not raw resid_post** (likely cause of L11's anomalous spectrum). Layers 0/3/6/9 are interior and correct — **the layer-6 headline is unaffected.**

**Wording/reporting fixes:** AE reframed "weak corroboration" → "raw-variance reconstruction artifact consistent with low ID" (#1); param-matched section now states h1 varies and drops "k is the only varying channel" (#2); filled matched-AE train_FVU for k=128/256 from existing JSON (#3); headline "stable across token position" → "TwoNN stable, MLE estimator-dependent" (#6).

Updated RESULTS.md, REPORT.md, PLAN.md, JOURNAL.md; renamed the review to `.addressed.md`; recreated STOP. ~235 min budget used.

**On track? yes — S1–S5c complete, all three reviews addressed, STOP written, no blocker.**
